## What happened

1. The first run of this role found two Red conflicts in the reader contract (a per-book root was
   assumed for a shared A4 leaf, and the A3 pictures were compared by index against the imposed
   order). Red r3 (commit c294f4b6) fixed both. This run built the reader code on the fixed
   contract.
2. The reader code passes its whole contract: R-P4-1 to R-P4-9, `Tests 10 passed (10)`.
3. The picture list version 4 (row Green 4b) cannot pass two committed expectations:
   - `__tests__/storytime-print-adversarial.test.ts` "gives zero picture rows for the shipped
     review week" (Phase 1 guard, commit 0ae1adf2) expects 0 rows for week 8.
   - R16 of `__tests__/storytime-print-contract-r3.test.ts` pins the exact 53-key object-count
     inventory; the 4 new week 8 rows add drum, mango, moon, and ostrich (57 keys).
   R4b-2 requires the 4 rows, so no implementation of version 4 passes both. This role does not
   edit a committed Red test.

## Code

Code commit `a2792002` (`feat(storytime-print): readers, picture check, and the readers PDF CLI
(Phase 4 Green)`), 4 files, 837 insertions, 2 deletions:
- `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/readers.ts` (new): `compileStorytimeReaders`. The workbook leaves
  impose the 3 strips of a reader with the page pairs 12/1, 2/11, 10/3, 4/9, 8/5, 6/7, two strips
  on each A4 leaf (one for each reader of the week), the dashed cut line at 148.5 mm, and the
  perforation 12 mm from the spine with the page parity. The color A3 output puts one reader page
  on each A3 page (297 x 420 mm, scale 3.0). `proof` prints "PICTURE MISSING"; `final` stops with
  the picture id (FR-5.6). The reader cover prints the title, "Sprout", "Storytime Advantage", and
  the week number, and a cover text that holds a CEFR word stops the build (FR-6.3).
- `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/picture-check.ts` (new): stage 1 of the picture stages (FR-9):
  `checkStorytimePicture` and `DEFAULT_GRAY_PIXEL_THRESHOLD = 0.02`. The color file must be PNG,
  8-bit, sRGB, 3 channels, no alpha; the line art must be PNG, 8-bit, grayscale, opaque, with ink
  and with at most 2 percent of its pixels in the gray band 32 to 223; the manifest must name the
  two files, with the file SHA-256 and the pixel size.
- `dashboard/scripts/storytime/make-readers-pdf.ts` (new): `--level --weeks [--proof|--final]
  [--workbook|--a3-color] [--version] [--out]`. `--out` must resolve inside
  `<home>/Desktop/print-ready/storytime/`; the shared `checkStorytimeOutputContainment` rejects a
  link or a dangling link, and an existing output file stops the build with exit 2.
- `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/student-book.ts`: `fontFaceCss` is exported, so the reader
  document loads the same Andika faces.

Uncommitted work of row Green 4b (in the working tree):
- `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/pictures.ts`: `STORYTIME_PICTURE_LIST_VERSION = 4` and the rows of
  `block.days[].paper` and `benchmark.paper.items`, with the reuse rule (a word that weeks 1 to 7
  hold keeps its row).
- `content/storytime/l2/print/pictures.json` and `pictures.md`: 196 rows (192 rows of weeks 1 to 7
  byte-equal to version 3, and the 4 week 8 rows moon, mango, ostrich, drum), header "Version 4".
  The rerun `npx tsx scripts/storytime/print-pictures.ts --level 2` exits 0.

