## Mutants

11 applied, 8 caught, every restore `cmp` OK (`jr-green-75cc5e54-mutants.txt`, one run in one
wrapper). M1 the 12/1 pair swapped to 1/12: R-P4-2 fails. M2 the back slots reversed: R-P4-2
fails. M3 every perforation on the left edge: R-P4-2 fails. M4 final mode prints the placeholder:
R-P4-5 fails. M5 the A3 output uses the `-line` file: R-P4-4 fails. M8 the gray-fill check
removed: R-P4-9 fails. M9 the manifest SHA-256 check removed: R-P4-9 fails. M10 the week 8 rows
dropped: R4b-2, R4b-3, R4b-5, and R16 fail. M6 (the alpha check removed), M6b (the 3-channel
fallback removed), and M7 (the CMYK check removed) survive, because another rule rejects the same
file with a message that the test regex accepts; the measured evidence that the CMYK and the RGBA
files stay rejected is in the mutants file. No wrong file passes.

